This paper investigates the normalized ground state solution for the given biharmonic Choquard type equation \begin{align*}
  \left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
  \Delta^2u-\beta\Delta u=\lambda u+\left(\frac{1}{|x|^\mu}*F(u)\right)f(u),
  \quad\mbox{in}\ \ \mathbb{R}^4,
  \displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}F(u),
  \displaystyle u\in C^0(\mathbb{R}^4).
  \end{array}
  \right.
  \end{align*} where $\beta$ is a constant, $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}$, $x\in\mathbb{R}^4$, $\mu\in [0,4)$ and $F$ is a function that satisfies certain properties. Under the condition that $(\Delta+\lambda)u=0$ outside a bounded domain, we establish the existence of a normalized ground state solution for this equation.
